+# Native Vice City Metal port
+
+Built and installed on 2026-10-17. This is a separate Apple Silicon reVC port, based on the re3 miami branch (a16fcd8d), with the native Metal backend and mod code carried over from regta-upstate. The original GTA III checkout/runtime and CrossOver Vice City folder are retained.
+
+## Start
+
+Open `Launch Vice City Metal.command` in this folder, or run:
+
+```sh
+cd /Users/jaymeeduardo/Documents/revc-metal-run
+./reVC_metal
+```
+
+Choose New Game for the story or Start Free Roam for the Vice City road selector. F7 toggles the trainer (on an Apple keyboard, Fn-F7 may be needed). Graphics > Advanced graphics exposes Metal MSAA, temporal smoothing, MetalFX, reflection resolution and the RT features. Settings are stored in reVC.ini; saves belong to this runtime's userfiles folder.
+
+## Ported
+
+- Native Metal rendering, 2x/4x MSAA, MetalFX and temporal smoothing/motion vectors.
+- Textured car/environment/ped reflections, owner exclusion, shadows, ambient occlusion, indirect light, lamps, glass and wet roads.
+- Native Modloader, trainer, Classic Axis, SA vehicle camera and 60 FPS limiter.
+- LocalDent deformation of existing car geometry, cabin intrusion/occupant injury, engine stalls/retries and per-car dirt.
+- Free-roam selector generated from VC's own land paths (12,288 road/footpath segments). Traffic uses VC's nine vehicle classes, with approximately 3% police and 7% taxis.
+- Citroen SM 1972: the archive's actual Vice City Virgo DFF/TXD/COL and author handling/colours/IDE, rather than the GTA III version.
+- Realistic Weights: 14 heavy-vehicle mass overrides applied to VC handling rows, preserving other VC handling fields.
+- Native custom-script support; CLEO directories are prepared. No GTA III compiled scripts were copied.
+
+Legacy III names on the native plugin marker files/INI files are intentional: the built-in compatibility loader recognizes those filenames. They do not require executing Windows ASI code.
+
