+# Native Metal MSAA and temporal history
+
+The scene framebuffer uses native Metal 2D multisample colour, depth, velocity and reflection attachments. Geometry pipelines use the same raster sample count, including masked/scissored clears. Samples remain stored across encoder/submission breaks. A scene resolve runs before ray tracing, MetalFX and the HUD. It averages colour coverage and selects the nearest depth sample for motion, signed actor identity and reflection direction. Reflection weights include the selected surface's sample coverage; object tags are never averaged. Resize and sample-count changes rebuild the private multisample textures. The HUD and post-processing remain single-sample.
+
+Default: 2x. Advanced graphics > Metal MSAA offers Off, 2x and 4x. `RenderMSAAIdx=0/1/2` persists this setting; `RenderMSAA=1/2/4` is also accepted for direct INI configuration. Unsupported sample counts fall back to a supported count. The FPS overlay reports the actual scene sample count. Changing the count resets temporal history. MetalFX and temporal AA remain independent, enabled settings; MSAA does not restore detail lost to a reduced render scale and does not supersample reflected geometry or alpha-tested textures.
+
+Temporal metadata records signed actor identity, depth, dynamic shadow coverage and luminance. Matching reprojected cars/pedestrians retain history. Identity changes, newly exposed background, static depth mismatches and changed shadow coverage reject stale samples. Large changes of reflected radiance receive partial reactivity rather than blanket rejection. Spatial edge smoothing only handles rejected/disoccluded pixels. Previous bone matrices provide animated limb motion in addition to the previous world transform. Actor IDs recycle only after their old history is no longer eligible.
+
+Validation uses hidden windows and actual Metal command encoders with `MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1`:
+
+- `tools-mtl/msaa-test.mm`: 1x has 0 partial-coverage pixels, 2x has 73, 4x has 101. Tests overlapping foreground/background surfaces, exact signed tags, reflection coverage, submission breaks, resize and sample-count transitions.
+- `tools-mtl/skin-motion-test.mm`: combined rigid/limb velocity is 0.199951 / -0.149902 versus expected 0.20 / -0.15, with exact actor identity.
+- `tools-mtl/mfx-reactive-test.cpp`: matching actors retain temporal history; disocclusions, crossed actors, changed static depth and shadows reject it. Existing sharpening bounds remain covered.
+- `tools-mtl/rt-rectangle-composite-test.mm`: production car composite and reactive edge path match the reference with zero pixel differences.
+- `tools-mtl/difftest.mm`: all 15 shader pairs match, including disabled-attribute mode.
+
+These checks establish the native sampling/resolve and motion/history contracts. Final gameplay appearance, ghosting and frame rate still require checking the installed build in the game. No 60 FPS guarantee is implied.
+
+Implementation reference: Apple's [MSAA sample](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/metal/improving-edge-rendering-quality-with-multisample-antialiasing-msaa) describes native multisample targets and custom resolves. This renderer uses a custom resolve to preserve non-colour scene metadata.
