+# Quality-preserving Metal optimizations
+
+The October 17 retained runtime log reported 35.5 ms GPU time. That is not a live profile of this build, and synthetic timings below do not establish an in-game frame rate.
+
+- Large reflection skin meshes (at least 16,384 vertices) use four libdispatch jobs. Each job performs independent vertex arithmetic; engine objects and Metal encoding remain on the render thread. Smaller meshes keep the serial path. Skinning is synchronous before its output is consumed. Invalid joint indices still reject the pose.
+- Reflection argument-buffer residency resources are deduplicated only when their surface records change. Unchanged frames reuse the retained resource list. Streaming/replacement rebuilds the list with the argument buffer; shutdown clears it. GPU resources still receive `useResources` every trace.
+- The shadow/light kernel avoids zeroing outputs it subsequently overwrites, while preserving every early-return write. Position history is written once at its final value. Lights outside their influence or behind the surface reject before square root/normalization.
+
+No resolution, sample count, effect, reflection distance, model population or texture setting is reduced.
+
+Validation on Apple M1:
+
+- `tools-mtl/skin-parallel-test.cpp`: byte-identical serial/parallel poses at small counts, scheduling boundary and 32,768 vertices; invalid-joint rejection. 16k vertices: approximately 0.087 ms serial versus 0.058-0.061 ms threaded; 32k: 0.173-0.176 ms versus 0.076-0.082 ms. This measures CPU posing only.
+- `tools-mtl/rt-lossless-perf-test.mm`: production Metal shadow/light kernel compared with the pre-optimization kernel from commit `a534fa5`, all four output textures, six effect flag combinations including combined lighting, sky and degenerate normals. Maximum float error 0. Synthetic 512x256 GPU timing: 0.877 ms baseline versus 0.781 ms optimized in the final run. Run with Metal API Validation enabled. Save the baseline with `git show a534fa5:src/extras/metalfx/MetalRT.cpp > /tmp/regta-rt-before-perf.cpp` and pass that path to the test.
+- `tools-mtl/rt-shadow-history-test.mm`: 16 jitter phases, surface rejection and 4 cm dynamic contact occluder pass.
+- `tools-mtl/rt-ped-reflections-test.mm`: textured ray hits, own-car exclusion, other cars/peds, geometry replacement and retained resource cache invalidation pass with Metal API Validation.
+- Native Metal executable builds. Real gameplay performance and visual approval remain unverified.
