+# Performance fix parity audit
+
+2026-10-18. Audited GTA III and Vice City, Metal and OpenGL sources/builds.
+
+| Fix requested from the earlier profile | Both games |
+|---|---|
+| Environment-map overhead | Already skips the legacy map while textured ray reflections are active; legacy fallback refreshes on alternate frames. Reflection resolution, trace geometry and ray counts are preserved. |
+| Expensive mouse hover check | Removed the remaining every-15-frame `GLFW_HOVERED` query. State is initialized after callback registration, updated by enter/leave callbacks and refreshed on focus regain. Input motion/button sampling remains active. |
+| Per-string text logging | Already disabled unless `REGTA_DEBUG_TEXT=1` is explicitly set. No runtime text debug logs were present to clean up. |
+| Forced Retina framebuffer | Already follows each game's own INI (`re3.ini` / `reVC.ini`). Metal uses requested pixels rather than automatically multiplying by display backing scale; Retina=1 remains available. |
+| Duplicate sun shadows | Existing dark car/heli/pole blobs are skipped when traced sun shadows are visible. Pedestrian blob shadows, blood, marks and light pools remain. |
+| Stale trainer text on radar | Existing depth/stencil clear before HUD composition is retained. |
+| GPU diagnostics | Existing opt-in pass timing and actual RT/MetalFX GPU timing are retained. |
+
+Validation: both Metal and both OpenGL executables build successfully. A hidden native test exercises production cursor/focus callbacks and confirms actual Metal drawable requests of 48x48, 96x96 and 32x24 are respected. No game was launched. This verifies source/build/native fixture behavior, not a measured gameplay FPS gain or complete shadow/HUD appearance.
+
+Runtime settings at audit: both use Retina=0 and RenderScaleIdx=0 (100%). GTA III uses RenderMSAAIdx=1; Vice City uses RenderMSAAIdx=2. Installation preserves INI bytes, reflection settings, geometry and texture detail. No resolution/detail reduction is part of this update.
