new file mode 100644
index 00000000..ac30673f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/RAY_REFLECTION_MATERIALS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Ray reflection materials
+
+Reflection rays retain mesh/triangle identity and barycentric coordinates. Per-mesh Metal argument-buffer records provide triangle UVs, original game textures, and material tint. Car instances carry independent primary/secondary paint colours, so shared geometry no longer forces one cached paint colour onto every instance. UV/texture records are immutable between model/topology changes, and updated argument buffers are replaced to preserve in-flight frames.
+
+Nearby loaded cars are collected independently of the main camera. The nearest 24 loaded pedestrians within 25 metres are also eligible; actors already collected this frame reuse their posed geometry. Off-camera skinned actors update their bone matrices. Occupants share their vehicle's reflection owner, allowing receiving-car panels to exclude their own cabin and occupants.
+
+Materials with textures are shaded directly at the ray hit, including off-screen hits. Untextured hits can use current-frame colour only when projected depth matches the hit; otherwise material colour remains the fallback. Geometry outside the registered/loaded world is not available to trace. Alpha-cutout traversal is not implemented.
+
+The reflection-direction attachment uses half floats instead of 8-bit channels. Ray images now default to full scene resolution (one ray per marked scene pixel), removing the former shared 2x2 sample blocks. `RenderRTHalfRes=1` opts back into reduced resolution for performance. This shared RT resolution also affects shadow tracing cost. Scene resolution still follows render scale; MSAA does not supersample reflected geometry. The legacy environment coat and its extra world render are skipped while ray reflections are active; the ray composite carries the full material weight at the default RT strength of 0.5. Car clear-coat reflections are composited after local diffuse shadowing and ambient occlusion, so these factors cannot darken the reflected image. The RT coat uses a 0.60 to 0.90 Fresnel range multiplied by the material shininess, preserving matte trim. Dynamic contact shadows use a small independent ray offset so the larger static-map offset does not detach shadows from tires.
+
+The GPU tests in tools-mtl/rt-ped-reflections-test.mm cover direct UV texture samples, independent paint colours on shared models, rejection of foreground colour leakage, own-vehicle exclusion, animated actors, and resource replacement. tools-mtl/rt-shadow-history-test.mm covers jitter history and a dynamic occluder 4 cm above the road.
+
+For optional diagnostics, launch with REGTA_RT_PROBE=1 and create rt_probe in the runtime folder. One trace exports depth, directions and output through GPU blits into shared buffers. The output alpha for that diagnostic frame labels sky/static/car/unowned-dynamic hits as 0/1/2/3. Normal output alpha is unchanged. Exported rows use the renderer's GL orientation. Diagnostic readback waits for that frame and should not be enabled for performance measurements.
+
+Filtered rectangle reads in the GLSL-to-Metal translator normalize pixel coordinates before sampling the underlying Metal 2D texture. This is necessary for the car composite: unconverted coordinates sampled the wrong texels and destroyed the reflected image. Constant-buffer sizes are rounded to 16 bytes to match Metal struct alignment.
+
+`tools-mtl/rt-rectangle-composite-test.mm` runs the production car composite with nonuniform full- and half-resolution images through the actual Metal backend and compares every output pixel against an OpenGL reference. Before the conversion fix, maximum byte error was 255 and mean error 93.132161; after it, both are zero, with Metal API Validation enabled. This establishes correct compositing, not final in-game visual approval.
+
+Opaque vehicles receive stable per-clump clean/light/heavy dirt states (40/40/20 distribution). Smooth car-space grime collects low on the body and near wheel stations; coverage attenuates diffuse paint, highlights and reflection weight. Transparent/named glass is excluded. This is a spawn-time appearance variation, not dynamic dirt accumulation or a washing system. Untextured non-paint black materials (including the installed HD Stallion fabric roof with specular 0.6), named fabrics, rubber and interior materials receive no paint clear coat; editable black body paint keeps its coat.
+
+Temporal AA now validates reprojected depth and signed actor identity rather than rejecting all dynamic pixels. Matching car/pedestrian surfaces retain history, newly exposed background rejects stale actor pixels, and moving shadows reject history only where coverage changes. Large changes of reflected radiance receive partial reactivity. Previous bone poses supply animated limb motion. Spatial edge AA remains limited to rejected/disoccluded pixels. Native Metal MSAA independently provides 2x/4x geometry coverage before RT and MetalFX; the nearest depth sample supplies intact motion/owner tags, and reflection weights account for partial coverage. See METAL_MSAA_AND_TEMPORAL_AA.md for validation and limits.
+
+Advanced graphics now exposes "RT reflection/shadow resolution": 100%, 50%, or 25% of scene width and height. These correspond to one ray sample per 1x1, 2x2, or 4x4 scene block. Changes apply on the next frame, rebuild RT targets and invalidate temporal history. `RenderRTResolutionIdx=0/1/2` persists the selection and takes precedence over the legacy `RenderRTHalfRes` key regardless of INI order. Default is 100%. Lower choices affect the shared reflection/shadow/AO/light tracing grid, not just cars. Texture compression cannot replace this ray-count tradeoff.
