+# ZMenuIII on native macOS
+
+Place `ZMenuIII.asi` and `ZMenuIII.ini` from the supplied ZMenu package in the
+game's `scripts` folder. The existing ASI discovery path recognizes that name
+and enables the native trainer compatibility subset in `ZMenuPort.cpp`.
+
+The supplied ZMenuIII 23.08.10.1 binary is Windows PE/x86, SHA-256
+`d92998764047c39d5241783fd0162408ae248a2ad354def2c592c63aa4a3af13`.
+REA `open_binary` established its format and architecture. It cannot execute
+inside the native macOS arm64 game. Its Windows DLL dependencies and asset
+scripts are not loaded; this is a new native implementation of common trainer
+functions, not a complete port of ZMenu or an emulation layer.
+
+Press F7 in gameplay. Use arrows or numpad 8/2 to select an option, Enter or
+numpad 5 to apply, and Tab/Backspace/numpad 0/F7 to close. For Spawn vehicle,
+Enter opens a paged browser of every installed automobile definition (52 in the
+current data set, including emergency/gang cars, trucks, tank, RC Bandit and Dodo).
+Up/down selects, left/right changes page, Enter spawns ahead when ground is available,
+and Tab returns to the parent trainer menu. The list comes from the live model registry. Gameplay continues while the trainer is
+open, with player controls temporarily disabled.
+
+Implemented: god mode, never wanted, unlimited ammunition, health and armour,
+all weapons, wanted-level clearing, money, vehicle repair, vehicle spawning,
+sunny/normal weather, and advancing time. The original INI's `AlwaysGodMode`,
+`NeverWanted`, `UnlimitedAmmo`, and F1-F12 `MenuToggle` values are imported.
+Other original settings and features are unsupported. Changes to health,
+weapons, money and vehicles affect the current game and may be saved normally.
+
+The loader logs `native compatibility subset active` and explicitly states
+that the Windows PE/x86 code is not executed. Removing `ZMenuIII.asi` disables
+this compatibility subset on the next launch. The source download is unchanged.
